WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.010
What is Sun-chul doing?

2
00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:21.070
Sun-chul...

3
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.480
- He's studying. - Yeah.

4
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.590
- Isn't it midterms? - Yeah.

5
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.329
To show his grandpa,

6
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:30.439
he's working pretty hard.

7
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.300
- Right. - Yeah.

8
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.399
But why did you guys come over

9
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.730
and hole up here?

10
00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.369
Why aren't you studying together?

11
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.849
We were just about to leave.

12
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:43.810
No...

13
00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:45.790
Let's go.

14
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.320
Um... Grandpa.

15
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.590
If Sun-chul is too busy to come,

16
00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:55.860
we'll keep coming over instead.

17
00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.380
Yeah.

18
00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.690
Oh.

19
00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.300
Let's go.

20
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.630
Hey, you little rascals.

21
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:11.720
Did you guys

22
00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.940
eat properly?

23
00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.270
Hey, I still don't think this is going to work.

24
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.139
Why? What's wrong?

25
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.189
I mean, he said he'd contact us when he found the knife,

26
00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.519
but we haven't heard anything yet.

27
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.169
That guy Yoon Jiamin will figure something out.

28
00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:34.389
Leaving your best friend of 10 years

29
00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:37.289
in the hands of a junior you barely know,

30
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.739
and just waiting for a call, don't you feel ashamed?

31
00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.269
I feel like total crap about it too.

32
00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:42.889
Stop acting like you're the only loyal one.

33
00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:44.680
You knew this would happen too, that's why you asked him.

34
00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:47.419
If you don't want to go, then don't.

35
00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.030
I'm going even if I have to go alone. Damn it.

36
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.409
That's playing dirty, you punk.

37
00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.640
Damn it, you heard what the doctor said too.

38
00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.050
Grandpa.

39
00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.929
It wouldn't be surprising if he passed away

40
00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.440
at any moment now.

41
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.499
At least the last image Grandpa sees of Sun-chul,

42
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.260
even if he's not a f***ing excellent person,

43
00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.510
shouldn't be of a piece of trash, right?

44
00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.800
Bastard, how could you say... damn it.

45
00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.550
Let's go get our Grandpa's medical fees

46
00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.660
back.

47
00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.999
Yeah, that's what we should do.

48
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.849
Hey, and f***, that little bastard Chae Sun-ho,

49
00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:36.780
and the money from selling our standing army imported car,
f***, we need to get that back too.

50
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.060
Idiot.

51
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.140
Punk.

52
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.620
Hey, damn it.

53
00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.959
(3rd Period: English - Singular Form)

54
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.060
(National Language. 3rd Period: English - Singular Form. Math.)

55
00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.929
(Those who want to study, gather around!)

56
00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.100
(Hwang Min-hyun)

57
00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.399
(Han Ji-eun)

58
00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.670
(Cha Woo-min)

59
00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.680
(Lee Jong-hyun)

60
00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:20.280
(Shin Soo-hyun)

61
00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.620
(Yoon Sang-jeong, Gong Do-yu)

62
00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.760
"Study Group"

63
00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.750
Let go.

64
00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:46.890
Damn it.

65
00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.510
Let go, strawberry head. Damn it.

66
00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.959
Try saying that again.

67
00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:58.630
What?

68
00:03:58.631 --> 00:04:00.160
"You can do it, you can do it, rehabilitated person"?

69
00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.389
I am different from those idiots

70
00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.459
Jang Bi-hwan and Gook Gwan-woo.

71
00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.859
A detective just threatened them a little,

72
00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.830
and they f***ing tucked their tails between their legs immediately.

73
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:10.529
Juvenile detention center?

74
00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.979
So what if I get a record? I'll just treat it like adding stars.

75
00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.589
So spit it out quickly.

76
00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:17.230
Tell me what the hell you guys are plotting by coming in here.

77
00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:19.100
Damn it.

78
00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:28.580
Damn it.

79
00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.460
Damn it.

80
00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:37.610
Hey.

81
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.190
Looking at your uniform, you must be from Heukchang High School.

82
00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.069
Never seen you around before.

83
00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.819
Wow, it's been a long time since

84
00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:45.539
I've played hide-and-seek with a girl.

85
00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.840
That thing you're holding

86
00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:49.670
is a dangerous item that would make girls jealous.

87
00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.280
She seems to know something.

88
00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.970
Damn it, let go, you pervert!

89
00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.569
Damn it, so embarrassing.

90
00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.330
F***.

91
00:05:06.331 --> 00:05:08.509
Hey, you've got a pretty face.

92
00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.279
Turns out you have a stubborn personality.

93
00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.180
F***, I told you to let go!

94
00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.100
Keep it up.

95
00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.880
Seeing that look of disgust in your eyes

96
00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.220
turn into fear

97
00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.970
is the most thrilling part for me.

98
00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.250
Trash.

99
00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.240
You're going to pass out.

100
00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.350
Looks like it's locked from the inside.

101
00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:39.189
What about Joon and Ji-woo?

102
00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.439
Still can't reach them?

103
00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.959
Yeah, both of them disconnected at almost the same time.

104
00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.070
I hope nothing happened.

105
00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:47.580
Not hearing a response.

106
00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:49.729
Hey, Yoon Jiamin.

107
00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:51.570
- Yoon Jiamin! - He is answering.

108
00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:53.120
Jiamin.

109
00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.659
Se-hyun, why is it like this?

110
00:05:56.660 --> 00:05:59.050
- Hey, Jiamin. - Yeah.

111
00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:01.720
Hello.

112
00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:04.540
(Teacher Lee Han-kyung)
Jiamin.

113
00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.530
Teacher Han-kyung?

114
00:06:06.531 --> 00:06:09.760
Yes, are you preparing well for the exams?

115
00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.819
It's nothing major.

116
00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:14.329
It's just that there's a slight error

117
00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:15.370
in the test papers I handed out earlier today.

118
00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.690
Can you open it and take a look right now?

119
00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.780
Ah, right now?

120
00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.459
Why? Are you outside?

121
00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.290
No, of course I'm at home.

122
00:06:27.980 --> 00:06:28.980
Wait a moment.

123
00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.880
(Yoon Jiamin)

124
00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:15.860
Hello.

125
00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:17.560
Hello.

126
00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:21.060
- Huh, what's wrong with the phone? - Oh.

127
00:07:21.680 --> 00:07:22.660
Where did she go?

128
00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.330
What? What did you say?

129
00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:27.120
Jiamin.

130
00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:28.440
Ji-woo?

131
00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:29.800
"Ji-woo"?

132
00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:31.409
What's wrong with Ji-woo?

133
00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:32.569
N-nothing.

134
00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:35.149
Teacher, I'll call you back a bit later.

135
00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:36.230
Oh, okay.

136
00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.210
Hey Yoon Jiamin, are you going to take much longer?

137
00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:55.309
Damn it, Hee-won.

138
00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.629
Adjust this to the roof.

139
00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:57.490
Okay.

140
00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.109
What is this...

141
00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.539
Did it bump into something?

142
00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.200
What the, no it didn't.

143
00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:16.740
(Hee-won's)
Is it Hee-won's?

144
00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:20.270
What should we do?

145
00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.340
It seems we've been caught, right?

146
00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:26.570
What should we do?

147
00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:28.689
I hope everyone is okay.

148
00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.009
No one is reachable.

149
00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:31.670
- What should we do? - Hee-won.

150
00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.420
Let's at least head over there first.

151
00:08:33.421 --> 00:08:34.900
- Where? - To save them.

152
00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:36.790
Hee-won, pack your things quickly.

153
00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.160
Hey.

154
00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.390
Go tell those standing army kids to go home.

155
00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.270
Understood.

156
00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:17.080
Why are you here again?

157
00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:20.220
Tell me.

158
00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:21.520
Why did you kill someone?

159
00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.889
We got into an argument, and I did it in a fit of anger.

160
00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:28.630
So you really killed him?

161
00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:32.260
Nothing to worry about.

162
00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:35.390
You just need to say 'I am the culprit' and that's it.

163
00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.780
The company will hire a lawyer to handle it for you.

164
00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.450
We will take care of the rest.

165
00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:44.480
You just stay there for 3 years, and when you get out,

166
00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.130
become one of us.

167
00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.120
Everyone's happy, right?

168
00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:05.890
(YB Group Deputy: Kim Sun-chul)

169
00:10:05.891 --> 00:10:07.150
Take this.

170
00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.380
And take out the thing inside there.

171
00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.220
The thing in your inner pocket.

172
00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.070
Absolutely no one is forcing you.

173
00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.370
The choice is yours.

174
00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.639
Yes. I killed him.

175
00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.640
Because of an argument, in a fit of anger?

176
00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:57.910
Yes.

177
00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:02.169
'In a fit of anger, stabbed him 3 times', right?

178
00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:03.030
Yes.

179
00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:06.380
I can't stand this. I'm going crazy.

180
00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:09.860
Then where is your knife?

181
00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:12.979
I threw it away.

182
00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:13.900
Threw it where?

183
00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:19.169
The lawyer will tell you.

184
00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.649
So you're saying,

185
00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.679
because of an argument, in a fit of anger,

186
00:11:22.680 --> 00:11:25.039
you stabbed him 3 times and killed a person.

187
00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:26.780
And as for the whereabouts of the knife, we have to wait for the lawyer to say?

188
00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:28.360
Yes.

189
00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:29.850
I'm sorry.

190
00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.720
Why apologize to me?

191
00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.520
But is it really okay to be this easy?

192
00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:52.260
What?

193
00:11:52.261 --> 00:11:55.470
Is it really okay to just easily give up your life like this?

194
00:11:58.010 --> 00:11:59.070
I'm sorry, but...

195
00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:01.750
There is only one stab wound.

196
00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.870
W-wait a minute.

197
00:12:07.570 --> 00:12:09.320
I think I made a mistake.

198
00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:12.330
- At that moment... - Fine. I get it.

199
00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.550
I'll ask you for the very last time.

200
00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:18.899
Make the choice yourself.

201
00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.530
Think carefully before you answer.

202
00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:25.460
Did you really kill someone?

203
00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.920
I need to see my grandson become an excellent person

204
00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:32.759
so I can die in peace.

205
00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:34.080
Aren't you going to study?

206
00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:42.000
Hey.

207
00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.710
You shouldn't be staying here right now, right?

208
00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:49.389
Let that girl go.

209
00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:52.020
Are you giving me orders now?

210
00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.350
Damn it.

211
00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:02.870
Damn it.

212
00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.849
Since you've decided to resist,

213
00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.440
at least bring your brothers along.

214
00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.940
You think you can take me on all by yourself?

215
00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:20.600
His brother is here, asshole.

216
00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:32.849
Don't laugh, punk.

217
00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.690
After this is over, you're dead too.

218
00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:36.220
Damn it.

219
00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:43.570
It hurts like hell, damn it.

220
00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.430
The knife.

221
00:13:50.540 --> 00:13:51.400
The knife.

222
00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:04.430
These idiots, they don't know what's important.

223
00:14:08.230 --> 00:14:09.160
Damn it.

224
00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.380
Hey, you're really dead now.

225
00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:51.650
Wouldn't it have been nice to just obediently follow orders and go to jail?

226
00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.100
Hey.

227
00:14:54.101 --> 00:14:56.980
Why bother using your brain? Damn it.

228
00:14:57.380 --> 00:14:59.470
Kicking away the benefits served right to your mouth.

229
00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:04.900
Shut up, you bastard.

230
00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:09.500
Why are all Yeonbaek Gang thugs exactly the same?

231
00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:34.440
Damn it.

232
00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:50.410
Damn it, I really didn't f***ing want to lose my temper with you little brats.

233
00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:53.110
You damn kids,

234
00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.529
you should have just obediently listened and done as you were told.

235
00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.440
Why must you insist on seeking death?

236
00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:04.340
That psycho, seriously.

237
00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:40.790
Aren't you that four-eyes nerd from back then?

238
00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:43.599
Psycho four-eyes,

239
00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.719
what that bastard is holding is the evidence.

240
00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:48.649
Crazy, are you Bruce Lee or something?

241
00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:50.420
What era is this to still bring up Bruce Lee?

242
00:16:55.850 --> 00:16:57.570
Don't insult Bruce Lee in front of me.

243
00:16:58.230 --> 00:16:59.150
Oh boy.

244
00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:13.180
Psycho four-eyes, your stance isn't bad.

245
00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:17.700
Yoon Jiamin.

246
00:17:22.180 --> 00:27:24.990
Nunchucks are not meant for actual combat.

247
00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:27.800
Especially when you're using such heavy ones...

248
00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:35.930
- What the hell is this? - That?

249
00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.960
That's a 100-won aluminum nunchuck.

250
00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:43.709
Looks like you beating up the talent scout wasn't just talk.

251
00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:46.420
Get ready, you're next.

252
00:17:47.070 --> 00:17:47.930
Okay.

253
00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.250
Bring it on.

254
00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.450
Damn it, psycho four-eyes.

255
00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:28.759
Hey, Bruce Lee.

256
00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:29.860
Are you panicked?

257
00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:33.179
What? You were supposed to show up like a savior

258
00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:34.840
and resolve everything!

259
00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:36.850
Things aren't going according to plan, are they?

260
00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:40.200
Sun-chul.

261
00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:43.830
How is it?

262
00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:47.170
Do you think just taking the evidence is enough?

263
00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:52.380
When given the chance to turn yourself in for a reduced sentence,
you should have been thankful.

264
00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:53.970
This is absurd.

265
00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.800
I heard you're really strong.

266
00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:00.480
I even brought nunchucks.

267
00:19:03.520 --> 00:19:05.000
But you're way too weak.

268
00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:06.460
What?

269
00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:09.870
With just this much power,

270
00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:12.710
you want to ruin a person's life?

271
00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:15.130
You bastard.

272
00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:29.269
Punching power generation can be divided into three types based on distance.

273
00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:30.539
From a slightly further distance,

274
00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:33.120
(Hanlim Gymnasium)
a punch thrown from about 10 inches away is called 'Cheok-jin' (Foot Power).

275
00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.009
And from a slightly closer distance,

276
00:19:35.010 --> 00:19:37.379
commonly known as the 1-inch punch, is called 'Cun-jin' (Inch Power).

277
00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:38.240
And lastly,

278
00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:42.769
a punch thrown from less than 1 inch away,

279
00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:45.470
(Uncle's Forbidden Technique: Move 4)

280
00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.299
the ultimate power generation:

281
00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:51.140
(0-Inch Punch: 'Bun-jin' / Fraction Power)

282
00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:26.730
Bro.

283
00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:30.420
Are you okay?

284
00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:42.450
Bro, let's go back to school and study together.

285
00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:47.940
Study?

286
00:20:47.941 --> 00:20:49.690
You want to study too, right?

287
00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:57.440
Can I do that?

288
00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:00.550
At this point,

289
00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.300
can I still pretend to be a normal student?

290
00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:07.140
That guy...

291
00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:12.020
I knew this would happen. Bastard.

292
00:21:17.910 --> 00:21:20.530
I'd love to kill you, but I can't do that.

293
00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:23.830
I hope you live a long, sick life, you trash.

294
00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:30.800
Hey, Piercings.

295
00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:35.449
It's just studying, why are you being so dramatic and walking on eggshells around others?

296
00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:37.610
Nobody really cares that much about you, okay?

297
00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:41.579
Hesitation is for before you do something bad.

298
00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:42.520
Got it?

299
00:21:51.410 --> 00:22:00.570
Hey...

300
00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:22.550
Right.

301
00:22:43.910 --> 00:22:44.960
F***.

302
00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:48.020
Which lunatic...

303
00:22:53.920 --> 00:22:55.270
Wow, who is this?

304
00:22:55.840 --> 00:22:56.949
Mr. Na Tae-man?

305
00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:58.320
You bastard...

306
00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:01.660
Not Mr. Na Tae-man, it's Detective Na Tae-man.

307
00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:05.080
I get inexplicably nervous when I see cops.

308
00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:07.550
Did you come alone?

309
00:23:09.110 --> 00:23:09.930
What do you want?

310
00:23:09.931 --> 00:23:12.749
What else would I want from a guy like you? To make you confess.

311
00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:15.110
The killer in the Ancheon Port murder case, Choo Sung-woong.

312
00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:17.250
What nonsense are you talking about?

313
00:23:17.990 --> 00:23:21.190
That Ancheon Port incident, Kim Sun-chul killed him, right?

314
00:23:22.430 --> 00:23:23.810
Hasn't he turned himself in yet?

315
00:23:26.230 --> 00:23:27.350
You're picking on an innocent person...

316
00:23:29.710 --> 00:23:31.470
Anyway, talking nicely is useless.

317
00:23:32.060 --> 00:23:34.550
Hey, confess honestly before I start using bad words.

318
00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.530
Ugh, this bastard.

319
00:23:48.200 --> 00:23:49.919
(Class 2-4 Yoon Jiamin)
I came to get my notebook.

320
00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:51.510
Just saw an opening.

321
00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:05.090
(Study Group Schedule)

322
00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:09.940
The destiny-deciding midterm exams are finally here.

323
00:24:12.390 --> 00:24:14.500
Stop looking at the answers, you pig brain.

324
00:24:30.180 --> 00:24:31.110
Here is the money you withdrew.

325
00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:37.170
Don't flip it over yet.

326
00:24:44.020 --> 00:24:45.780
Meteor Vocational High School's midterm exams

327
00:24:47.190 --> 00:24:49.220
will have unreasonably simple questions.

328
00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:57.219
Will that lack discriminatory power?

329
00:24:57.220 --> 00:24:59.950
You can hear the sound of eyes rolling, right?

330
00:25:00.710 --> 00:25:01.640
Not at all.

331
00:25:06.900 --> 00:25:08.479
Hey, question nine is 1.

332
00:25:08.480 --> 00:25:09.350
Question nine?

333
00:25:10.260 --> 00:25:11.969
Stop spouting nonsense. Question nine is 3.

334
00:25:11.970 --> 00:25:13.510
- I picked 3. - Right? - She's my type.

335
00:25:18.490 --> 00:25:19.740
Question nine is 5, right?

336
00:25:20.410 --> 00:25:21.310
Question nine is 5...

337
00:25:21.310 --> 00:25:22.280
I picked 3.

338
00:25:22.281 --> 00:25:23.509
I picked 3 too.

339
00:25:23.510 --> 00:25:26.920
I picked 3!

340
00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:28.080
3.

341
00:25:28.081 --> 00:25:29.679
I told you, you lunatic.

342
00:25:29.680 --> 00:25:31.200
No, question nine is 1.

343
00:25:31.650 --> 00:25:33.149
Right? Is it 3?

344
00:25:33.150 --> 00:25:34.899
Yeah, the answer to question nine is 3.

345
00:25:34.900 --> 00:25:35.870
Oh my god.

346
00:25:35.871 --> 00:25:37.309
Damn it.

347
00:25:37.310 --> 00:25:39.319
- Give it to me. - Did you pick 1?

348
00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:40.489
But I'm not necessarily right...

349
00:25:40.490 --> 00:25:41.829
- Idiot. - I picked 3, Se-hyun.

350
00:25:41.830 --> 00:25:44.009
- You picked 3? - Yeah, I got it right.

351
00:25:44.010 --> 00:25:45.889
(Class 1-4 Yoon Jiamin)
- Damn it. - I'm the same as you.

352
00:25:45.890 --> 00:25:47.940
- Why did I get question nine...
- We can check answers together from now on.

353
00:25:48.700 --> 00:25:49.979
Wait, why...

354
00:25:49.980 --> 00:25:51.780
I picked 3.

355
00:25:52.740 --> 00:25:54.160
Heave-ho, heave-ho.

356
00:25:55.650 --> 00:25:57.229
Is it 'ga-yu, ga-yu'?

357
00:25:57.230 --> 00:25:58.320
It's 'jia-you, jia-you' (cheer up/you can do it).

358
00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:00.869
You can do it, you can do it, rehabilitated person.

359
00:26:00.870 --> 00:26:05.689
The Juvenile Rehabilitation Project launched to prevent
the Yeonbaek Gang from injecting new blood.

360
00:26:05.690 --> 00:26:06.960
Listen to your bullshit.

361
00:26:07.510 --> 00:26:10.130
Have you been brainwashed by hanging around Na Tae-man?

362
00:26:10.570 --> 00:26:12.959
Gwang-hyun, you need to wake up.

363
00:26:12.960 --> 00:26:15.069
- You know what I mean, right? - What?

364
00:26:15.070 --> 00:26:17.639
So far, has any guy voluntarily said they want to do it?

365
00:26:17.640 --> 00:26:19.279
Because it's still in the initial stages.

366
00:26:19.280 --> 00:26:20.160
See?

367
00:26:20.770 --> 00:26:22.669
I told you so.

368
00:26:22.670 --> 00:26:25.909
If there's a guy like that, I'll give you my head.

369
00:26:25.910 --> 00:26:26.950
Hello everyone.

370
00:26:29.770 --> 00:26:31.330
I came here to change.

371
00:26:33.790 --> 00:26:34.700
Senior.

372
00:26:46.140 --> 00:26:47.240
Auntie.

373
00:26:47.730 --> 00:26:49.589
I heard you were discharged from the hospital today.

374
00:26:49.590 --> 00:26:50.760
How is your body feeling?

375
00:26:51.190 --> 00:26:52.579
I took this as an excuse to get a good rest.

376
00:26:52.580 --> 00:26:54.430
So my body actually feels better than before.

377
00:26:55.100 --> 00:26:57.700
You must have had a hard time taking care of the kids too.

378
00:26:58.300 --> 00:27:00.740
Although it's very tiring, it's a lot of fun.

379
00:27:01.990 --> 00:27:05.260
By the way, didn't they finish their exams today?

380
00:27:06.020 --> 00:27:08.449
Yes, they finished exams today.

381
00:27:08.450 --> 00:27:10.119
Why? What's wrong?

382
00:27:10.120 --> 00:27:12.079
Have you heard where our Jiamin

383
00:27:12.080 --> 00:27:14.230
went?

384
00:27:14.650 --> 00:27:16.849
He hasn't come home, and he's not answering my calls.

385
00:27:16.850 --> 00:27:18.479
Because exams ended today,

386
00:27:18.480 --> 00:27:20.249
he went out to hang out with his classmates.

387
00:27:20.250 --> 00:27:21.260
Went out to hang out?

388
00:27:22.130 --> 00:27:23.080
I see.

389
00:27:23.870 --> 00:27:27.340
But it would have been better if he didn't go anywhere today.

390
00:27:32.060 --> 00:27:32.920
Now is the time.

391
00:27:38.990 --> 00:27:40.639
I'm so bored. Let's play a round too.

392
00:27:40.640 --> 00:27:42.240
The person with the lowest score has to treat everyone to ice cream.

393
00:27:43.050 --> 00:27:44.209
Just the three of us?

394
00:27:44.210 --> 00:27:46.040
Let's go... hurry up.

395
00:27:52.280 --> 00:27:54.649
Oh, weakling, you're pretty good.

396
00:27:54.650 --> 00:27:55.959
Oh, quite impressive.

397
00:27:55.960 --> 00:27:57.000
Very impressive.

398
00:27:58.020 --> 00:27:59.210
Is it my turn?

399
00:28:00.520 --> 00:28:03.090
Watch this. Lee Joon heavy punch!

400
00:28:08.910 --> 00:28:10.719
- For the past ten years, - What are you doing?

401
00:28:10.720 --> 00:28:12.489
- I've done a hundred push-ups every day. - Stop him.

402
00:28:12.490 --> 00:28:13.919
That kid is in the baseball batting cage...

403
00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:15.379
Joon, no!

404
00:28:15.380 --> 00:28:17.810
That money is our study group's public funds!

405
00:28:18.830 --> 00:28:19.979
What?

406
00:28:19.980 --> 00:28:22.330
It would be better if he didn't go anywhere today?

407
00:28:22.720 --> 00:28:23.580
Why is that?

408
00:28:25.630 --> 00:28:28.439
There are days I absolutely never disturb Jiamin.

409
00:28:28.440 --> 00:28:30.599
Only 4 days a year.

410
00:28:30.600 --> 00:28:34.620
That's the days when the midterms and finals for both semesters end.

411
00:28:35.290 --> 00:28:37.849
Once he checks his answers, he gets a little weird.

412
00:28:37.850 --> 00:28:39.640
He can't concentrate on anything.

413
00:28:40.220 --> 00:28:41.300
A bit...

414
00:28:41.890 --> 00:28:43.509
Hey, Yoon Jiamin, you have to score below 300 points.

415
00:28:43.510 --> 00:28:44.629
You have to pretend it's a machine malfunction.

416
00:28:44.630 --> 00:28:46.130
That's the only way he'll believe it, understand?

417
00:28:46.590 --> 00:28:47.819
Let me go.

418
00:28:47.820 --> 00:28:49.780
Hard work will never betray me.

419
00:28:55.210 --> 00:28:57.180
Should I say he can't control his strength?

420
00:29:01.450 --> 00:29:03.239
Damn it, if we went according to the original plan,

421
00:29:03.240 --> 00:29:05.400
we should be eating all-you-can-eat Korean BBQ right now.

422
00:29:07.070 --> 00:29:09.069
- Sorry. - Forget it...

423
00:29:09.070 --> 00:29:10.949
The owner was about to change the machine anyway.

424
00:29:10.950 --> 00:29:11.940
Hey, Gochujang.

425
00:29:11.941 --> 00:29:14.169
If we're going to point fingers, you're the main culprit, okay?

426
00:29:14.170 --> 00:29:16.250
It's all because you kept throwing a tantrum, damn it.

427
00:29:18.600 --> 00:29:20.300
I'll open it for you.

428
00:29:20.720 --> 00:29:22.550
So stop being angry, okay?

429
00:29:23.130 --> 00:29:23.990
Okay.

430
00:29:25.860 --> 00:29:27.550
Eat up, my treat.

431
00:29:27.910 --> 00:29:29.740
It's already been paid for, how is it your treat?

432
00:29:38.970 --> 00:29:41.190
Is it because the results were worse than you expected?

433
00:29:41.880 --> 00:29:43.559
- What? - I mean the results of this exam.

434
00:29:43.560 --> 00:29:45.560
Weren't you acting like that because you were worried about your grades?

435
00:29:46.940 --> 00:29:47.800
Yes.

436
00:29:48.370 --> 00:29:49.560
I thought

437
00:29:50.500 --> 00:29:51.610
this time would be different.

438
00:29:54.040 --> 00:29:56.929
But there's one thing I can't understand.

439
00:29:56.930 --> 00:29:59.919
Couldn't you get 20 points just by guessing on the multiple-choice questions?

440
00:29:59.920 --> 00:30:01.760
How could he only average 10 points?

441
00:30:02.940 --> 00:30:05.689
Yoon Jiamin doesn't guess on questions he doesn't know.

442
00:30:05.690 --> 00:30:06.819
- Is he crazy? - Huh?

443
00:30:06.820 --> 00:30:07.720
Why?

444
00:30:07.721 --> 00:30:10.290
He believes that points gained from guessing don't belong to him.

445
00:30:11.150 --> 00:30:12.469
Oh my god.

446
00:30:12.470 --> 00:30:13.530
As expected of God Jiamin.

447
00:30:18.490 --> 00:30:20.640
Kids, I'll ask you a question.

448
00:30:21.000 --> 00:30:21.880
Okay.

449
00:30:24.530 --> 00:30:27.360
What happens when water boils?

450
00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:31.660
Alright, Yoon Jiamin.

451
00:30:32.150 --> 00:30:33.060
You try answering.

452
00:30:33.590 --> 00:30:34.450
Me?

453
00:30:38.030 --> 00:30:39.950
You can eat ramen.

454
00:30:41.130 --> 00:30:42.440
- Wrong. - Is that incorrect?

455
00:30:43.670 --> 00:30:44.620
The answer is

456
00:30:45.030 --> 00:30:46.889
nothing happens.

457
00:30:46.890 --> 00:30:48.529
- What? - Huh?

458
00:30:48.530 --> 00:30:50.589
Water has to reach its boiling point

459
00:30:50.590 --> 00:30:52.429
before it bubbles and starts to evaporate.

460
00:30:52.430 --> 00:30:53.789
But before that,

461
00:30:53.790 --> 00:30:55.270
the water's appearance doesn't change at all.

462
00:31:02.180 --> 00:31:03.140
So what?

463
00:31:04.010 --> 00:31:05.240
- Huh? - And then what?

464
00:31:08.030 --> 00:31:09.560
So what I mean is,

465
00:31:10.420 --> 00:31:12.990
before reaching the boiling point,

466
00:31:13.800 --> 00:31:16.769
people might think the water's appearance

467
00:31:16.770 --> 00:31:18.399
hasn't changed at all.

468
00:31:18.400 --> 00:31:19.280
But...

469
00:31:20.500 --> 00:31:22.840
if you consistently pour energy into something,

470
00:31:23.380 --> 00:31:25.880
it will produce a massive change.

471
00:31:26.700 --> 00:31:28.500
It's the same for both water and studying.

472
00:31:36.950 --> 00:31:39.300
This came up in a question I was reading yesterday.

473
00:31:43.540 --> 00:31:44.400
Here, have this.

474
00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:46.010
- Is it good? - Yeah.

475
00:31:51.890 --> 00:31:52.770
Hello.

476
00:31:55.200 --> 00:31:56.260
Dae-chul bro?

477
00:31:58.050 --> 00:32:01.090
I'm not with Sun-chul bro right now.

478
00:32:06.170 --> 00:32:08.120
Hey, you punk, why weren't you answering your phone?

479
00:32:08.670 --> 00:32:10.549
Come quickly, Grandpa is failing.

480
00:32:10.550 --> 00:32:12.639
I told you I have to go take my exam.

481
00:32:12.640 --> 00:32:14.719
The exam is about to start.

482
00:32:14.720 --> 00:32:16.609
Grandpa, please wait just a little longer.

483
00:32:16.610 --> 00:32:18.810
We'll take you over as soon as Sun-chul gets here.

484
00:32:23.280 --> 00:32:24.140
Grandpa.

485
00:32:27.850 --> 00:32:29.700
I can go by myself.

486
00:32:40.370 --> 00:32:42.230
Kim Sun-chul, you son of a bitch.

487
00:32:42.870 --> 00:32:44.799
Where do you think you're going after smashing our rice bowls?

488
00:32:44.800 --> 00:32:45.989
Damn it.

489
00:32:45.990 --> 00:32:48.009
Since you agreed to take the fall for Choo Sung-woong,

490
00:32:48.010 --> 00:32:51.170
you have to say you killed that person until the day you die!

491
00:32:51.940 --> 00:32:54.690
I was about to become a Family member, how are you going to take responsibility?

492
00:32:57.250 --> 00:32:58.540
I don't have time.

493
00:32:59.090 --> 00:33:00.610
So shut your mouths and bring it on, all of you.

494
00:33:04.650 --> 00:33:05.550
Grandpa.

495
00:33:11.540 --> 00:33:12.970
Grandpa, you're ready, right?

496
00:33:17.000 --> 00:33:17.890
You're...

497
00:33:18.630 --> 00:33:20.290
Hurry up and get up, it's time.

498
00:33:21.250 --> 00:33:22.110
Okay.

499
00:33:24.180 --> 00:33:25.040
Okay.

500
00:33:31.200 --> 00:33:32.720
Kim Sun-chul, you punk.

501
00:33:35.060 --> 00:33:37.370
Hey, why are you only arriving now?

502
00:33:43.520 --> 00:33:44.640
Don't open the door.

503
00:33:47.090 --> 00:33:48.140
Move.

504
00:33:48.610 --> 00:33:49.709
Grandpa is...

505
00:33:49.710 --> 00:33:52.710
taking an exam.

506
00:33:54.430 --> 00:33:58.280
Teacher Han-kyung got last month's TOEIC test paper.

507
00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:37.000
Thank you.

508
00:34:57.380 --> 00:34:58.260
Just like that,

509
00:34:58.850 --> 00:35:00.990
our first high school exam was over.

510
00:35:02.170 --> 00:35:03.040
And

511
00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:08.390
Grandpa's last exam

512
00:35:09.170 --> 00:35:10.100
also came to an end.

513
00:35:23.440 --> 00:35:24.300
Child.

514
00:35:25.290 --> 00:35:27.300
If you see our Sun-chul,

515
00:35:27.720 --> 00:35:31.260
tell him for me how fun studying is.

516
00:35:31.690 --> 00:35:34.670
I think you'll definitely be able to do it.

517
00:35:46.920 --> 00:35:47.780
Grandpa.

518
00:35:48.360 --> 00:35:51.450
Sun-chul bro already knows

519
00:35:52.560 --> 00:35:54.080
that studying is a fun thing.

520
00:35:54.730 --> 00:35:55.590
Mm.

521
00:36:35.830 --> 00:36:36.920
A person,

522
00:36:37.840 --> 00:36:40.280
the moment they stop learning,

523
00:36:43.160 --> 00:36:45.370
life also comes to a standstill.

524
00:37:05.460 --> 00:37:06.340
Thank you...

525
00:37:08.580 --> 00:37:09.440
Jiamin.

526
00:37:46.480 --> 00:37:49.330
Grandpa.

527
00:37:55.790 --> 00:37:58.260
1, 2,

528
00:37:59.160 --> 00:38:00.060
3.

529
00:38:00.530 --> 00:38:03.379
Oh my god, I'm a genius, right?

530
00:38:03.380 --> 00:38:05.100
Me too.

531
00:38:08.410 --> 00:38:09.459
Gochujang head,

532
00:38:09.460 --> 00:38:10.859
why are you better at studying than me?

533
00:38:10.860 --> 00:38:12.269
Because my brain is better than yours!

534
00:38:12.270 --> 00:38:13.360
Damn it.

535
00:38:15.140 --> 00:38:17.820
So this is what a school rank number 1 report card looks like.

536
00:38:18.610 --> 00:38:20.370
I'm tied for first place with Ho-min, it's nothing.

537
00:38:22.020 --> 00:38:23.439
Hey, don't pretend to be humble.

538
00:38:23.440 --> 00:38:24.770
It's a total turn-off.

539
00:38:27.080 --> 00:38:27.940
Shh... he's...

540
00:38:37.870 --> 00:38:38.810
Oh my god.

541
00:38:38.811 --> 00:38:40.850
Yoon Jiamin is 209th out of 220 students.

542
00:38:42.650 --> 00:38:44.309
